ountry details for your evaluation."],[1486,"**Symptom:** A certificate's status is not synced to AWS after a revocation."],[1501,"**Symptom:** After editing a DMS in `jitp` mode, messages about that DMS update appear in the `lamassu-dlq` poison queue."],[1483,"**Symptom:** The CA registration stays in `REQUESTED` indefinitely."],[1492,"**Symptom:** The device receives `CLIENT_ID_REJECTED` when connecting to AWS IoT Core."],[1498,"**Symptom:** The Device Shadow is not updated when it should be."],[1495,"**Symptom:** The device's first MQTT connection in JITP mode fails or times out."],[1489,"**Symptom:** The forced disconnect does not terminate the device's MQTT session after revocation."],[2218,"**Tags**: associated labels."],[2187,"**Tags**: labels for classification and search."],[2209,"**Tags**: labels for organization and search."],[2200,"**Tags**: metadata to classify the key."],[2715,"**The helper pod stays `Pending` or `ContainerCreating` and `kubectl wait` times out.** Another pod still holds one of the claims; on block storage `kubectl describe pod pvc-migrate-helper` shows a `Multi-Attach error`. Check with `kubectl get pods -n $NAMESPACE` that `kms-0`, `va-0` and the new KMS and VA pods are gone, then re-run the wait."],[662,"**The response body is ignored.** Delivery checks the status code only, so the receiver may answer with any body."],[1442,"**The Thing name in AWS is the Common Name (CN) of the device's certificate.** This convention is fundamental for the firmware developer: the `/CN=` value the device includes in its CSR when enrolling becomes the ThingName it must identify itself with in all MQTT operations against AWS IoT Core."],[2718,"**The upgrade fails at the CA-to-KMS hook.** CA certificates that share a `subject_key_id` declare conflicting `engine_id`s. Resolve the conflict and re-run."],[2717,"**The upgrade fails at the database job.** The PostgreSQL role cannot create databases or schemas, or a schema migration aborted on duplicate CA I