g). The template is created once; later DMS edits never update its content. A DMS update that omits `metadata` or sends `null` keeps the stored metadata, so the connector key `lamassu.io/iot/{connector_id}` remains present and the attempt is still triggered. A body that supplies a `metadata` object replaces the stored metadata entirely: if that object does not carry the connector key, the key is dropped and the connector silently skips the DMS's future events. Once the template is attached, when a device with a certificate issued by that CA connects to AWS IoT Core for the first time, AWS executes the template automatically: it creates the Thing, registers the certificate and activates it."],[250,"K3s"],[271,"K3s ServiceLB implements each `LoadBalancer` Service with pods that reserve the Service ports on the node. On a single node, only one Service can therefore own port 80 and one can own port 443. The default K3s Traefik Service may already hold both ports."],[593,"Keep `failOpen: false` unless a documented risk assessment justifies otherwise."],[876,"Keep `true` to verify CSR key possession."],[595,"Keep at least two recovery administrators and test their access periodically."],[2077,"Keep enough overlap to renew a disconnected fleet."],[1215,"Keep initial EST server trust separate from identity consumer trust."],[709,"keep the complete CloudEvent unmodified;"],[1658,"Keep the device identifier, owning DMS and serial number as references for the result."],[1112,"Keep the result as `device.next.crt` and `device.next.key` until verified. Switch the pair through a coordinated operation in the device store or configuration; avoid temporarily exposing a certificate with another version's key."],[2073,"Keep the root out of daily operations, or with very restricted access."],[1958,"Keep the serial number, issuer, revocation reason, query time and evidence timestamps. An existing session may need explicit closure or reauthentication in the consumer; publishing revocation